@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# Live observation and exact native settlement
+
+`history_observation_poll` shares the immutable history snapshot cut and a bounded, contiguous worker observation
+sequence. Native source records carry mutation/context counters and actual native entry/leaf IDs. Source append,
+rewrite, deletion/reparent (rebuild), leaf and context changes remain observable. A lost/evicted journal cursor fails
+`history_observation_gap`. Direct mutable retained-payload rewrites discovered by coherent capture emit
+`native_untracked_rewrite`. Stop the affected projection and reopen after any incompatible source change or gap.
+
+`message_start`, `message_update`, `message_final` and `message_settlement` carry a native lifecycle identity scoped by
+worker, source, native Session, native context and initiating branch leaf. The identity is stamped before asynchronous
+display delivery; filtered or reordered stdout cannot change it. Tool results additionally carry the initiating
+assistant message identity when that exact native context has retained the call. An absent owner requires explicit
+failure/reopen, never pairing a reusable raw tool ID across contexts. Tool-owner associations are bounded to 4096.
+Final readable content supersedes partial reconstructions. Internal custom/configuration/provider state is not exposed.
+
+Settlement happens at AgentSession's actual append/no-append decision. An original object append association and
+the existing assistant entry Symbol provide authoritative IDs; no text, timestamp, hash or append adjacency joins
+are used. A native duplicate without an original-object association explicitly reports `no_entry` with
+`native_deduplicated_without_link`; this lifecycle appended no new entry and does not claim an old entry association.
+One-run contexts, classifier refusals, empty errors, consumed rewind results and replaced prompt generations report
+explicit no-entry reasons. A throwing native decision reports `failed`. Entries observed in memory report `observed`
+and **durability `not_attested`**. Ordinary append may be lazy or latch write failures; this API never promises durable
+recovery. Recoverable submission/commit receipts require a separate capability.
+
+Snapshot items include retained lifecycle associations so snapshot/live overlap can be excluded by exact identity.
+Those associations are process-local and bounded to 4096; eviction emits `native_settlement_evicted` and invalidates
+an existing derived projection. Old cold entries remain readable, with no invented historical live identity.
+Oversized or unrepresentable live data emits `native_live_gap`; no successful truncated live message is returned.
+Native observation does not cancel or recreate Interactions or execution, and does not alter collaboration callbacks.
